{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "שבתון זכרון תרועה", :translit "shabbaton zikhron teru'ah", :gloss "a solemn rest, a remembrance of teru'ah"} {:he "תקעו שופר בציון", :translit "tike'u shofar batziyon", :gloss "blow a shofar in Zion"} {:he "שבת שבציון תוקעין", :translit "shabbat shebatziyon toke'in", :gloss "on Shabbat in Zion they blow"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "שבת שבציון תוקעין", :spells "תקעו שופר בציון"}], :frame {:text "Shofar blowing on Rosh HaShanah does not override Shabbat except in the Temple, where it is performed even on Shabbat (Rosh HaShanah 29b). The phrase 'blow a shofar in Zion' (Joel 2:1) is read as an allusion that in Zion — the Temple — shofar is blown even on Shabbat.", :sources ["Rosh HaShanah 29b" "Joel 2:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "זכרון", :translit "zikhron", :gloss "remembrance"} {:he "אין זכרון לראשונים", :translit "ein zikhron larishonim", :gloss "there is no remembrance of the first ones"} {:he "אין זכרון לחכם עם הכסיל", :translit "ein zikhron lechakham im hakesil", :gloss "there is no remembrance of a wise man with the fool"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["זכרון" "אין זכרון לראשונים" "אין זכרון לחכם עם הכסיל"]}], :frame {:text "Three books are opened on Rosh HaShanah: the righteous are sealed immediately for life, the wicked for death, and the intermediate stand suspended until Yom Kippurim (Rosh HaShanah 16b). Solomon observes 'there is no remembrance of the first ones' (Ecclesiastes 1:11) and 'there is no remembrance of the wise man with the fool' (Ecclesiastes 2:16). Ba'al HaTurim reads the word 'זכרון' itself — the one positive occurrence corresponding to the intermediates who still need remembrance, the two negative 'אין זכרון' occurrences corresponding to the righteous and wicked who are already sealed and need no further remembrance.", :sources ["Rosh HaShanah 16b" "Ecclesiastes 1:11" "Ecclesiastes 2:16"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :rashei-tevot, :phrase "שבת שבציון תוקע